---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { languageMeta } from "../lib/languages";

const glossaries = await getCollection("glossaries");
const translations = await getCollection("translations");

const languages = glossaries
  .map((glossary) => {
    const lang = glossary.data.lang;
    const items = translations.filter((t) => t.data.lang === lang);
    return {
      lang,
      meta: languageMeta(lang),
      termCount: glossary.data.sections.reduce((total, section) => total + section.terms.length, 0),
      published: items.filter((t) => t.data.status === "published").length
    };
  })
  .sort((a, b) => a.meta.name.localeCompare(b.meta.name));

const totalPublished = languages.reduce((total, l) => total + l.published, 0);

const QUICK_LINKS = [
  {
    label: "Kickoff live stream",
    detail: "Friday 1pm UTC, YouTube",
    href: "https://youtube.com/live/UAxC5J4H2n0"
  },
  {
    label: "Discord",
    detail: "The #translation channel, where we work",
    href: "https://discord.gg/JFty3vbqRZ"
  },
  {
    label: "The forum",
    detail: "Where decisions get recorded",
    href: "https://forum.jiki.io/c/i18n/67"
  },
  {
    label: "The blog post",
    detail: "The full story of the Translatathon",
    href: "https://jiki.io/blog/translatathon"
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title="Jiki Translations"
  description="The Big Jiki & Exercism Translatathon: read the translations as they land, check the agreed glossaries, and tell us what sounds wrong."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="The Big Jiki & Exercism Translatathon"
    subtitle="Over the weekend of July 31st - August 2nd, we're translating Jiki and Exercism into as many languages as we can, together. This site is where the translations land for you to read and pull apart."
    image="/images/translatathon.webp"
  />

  <div class="lg-container grid gap-10 py-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_350px] lg:gap-[7%]">
    <article class="min-w-0">
      <div class="textual-content">
        <p class="rounded-xl border border-purple-200 bg-purple-50 p-5 text-[15px] italic">
          <strong>TL;DR</strong> We're translating Jiki and Exercism into as many languages as we can, over the weekend of
          <strong>Friday July 31st - Sunday August 2nd</strong>. Want to help? Join the
          <a href="https://youtube.com/live/UAxC5J4H2n0">kickoff live stream</a> at 1pm UTC on the Friday, or get stuck in
          on <a href="https://discord.gg/JFty3vbqRZ">Discord</a> and
          <a href="https://forum.jiki.io/c/i18n/67">the forum</a> any time over the weekend. Everyone who contributes gets
          an exclusive one-off Translatathon badge on both Jiki and Exercism!
        </p>

        <h2>What is this?</h2>

        <p>
          Most people in the world don't speak English, but most coding resources are only in English. So we're
          translating the whole of Jiki: the UI, the videos, the exercises, even the <strong>error messages</strong> you get
          from the programming language itself. And it's not just Jiki. Exercism is being translated too, using the same process
          and the same glossaries.
        </p>

        <p>
          We're using LLMs to do the translating, but using strict guides and glossaries that we create together. We run
          a loop: we translate, <strong>get human feedback</strong>, update the guides, and go again, until we're happy.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>This site is step two of that loop.</strong> Every translation we generate gets published here next to its
          English source, so you can see exactly what it says and exactly what it was meant to say. The
          <strong>glossary</strong> behind each language is published here too, so you can argue with the decisions rather
          than just the wording.
        </p>

        <p>
          Nothing here is final. That's the point. If it reads like a robot wrote it, we want to know before it ships.
        </p>

        <h2>What do I do?</h2>

        <p>
          <strong>Read something in your language and tell us when it sounds weird.</strong> That's genuinely it. You don't
          need to be technical, and you don't need to explain why. "This just sounds off" is really useful feedback. Some
          coding experience helps with the technical terms, but it isn't required.
        </p>

        <ol>
          <li>
            <strong>Pick your language</strong> from the list, and read its glossary. These are the technical terms we'll
            use consistently everywhere: what do we call a "function" or a "variable" in your language?
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Read the translations</strong> as they appear. Each one sits side by side with the English so you can
            see what it was translating.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Tell us what's wrong</strong> on the forum. This word sounds weird. Nobody actually says it that way.
            This sentence is too formal.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>We fix it and post a fresh version</strong>, and we repeat until everything reads naturally.
          </li>
        </ol>

        <p>
          Discussion happens on <a href="https://discord.gg/JFty3vbqRZ">Discord</a> over the weekend, but anything you agree
          needs to end up on <a href="https://forum.jiki.io/c/i18n/67">the forum</a>, because the forum is what the AI
          actually learns from.
        </p>

        <h3>What if my language isn't listed yet?</h3>

        <p>
          Post in <a href="https://forum.jiki.io/c/i18n/67">the forum</a> and we'll bootstrap it: a forum section for your
          language and a starting glossary to discuss. And if you know other native speakers who'd help out, get them to post
          too. The more people working on a language, the better it'll be.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <aside class="min-w-0 space-y-6">
      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5">
        <h2 class="text-[13px] font-bold tracking-[0.08em] text-gray-500 uppercase">Quick links</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1">
          {
            QUICK_LINKS.map((link) => (
              <li>
                <a href={link.href} class="-mx-2 block rounded-lg px-2 py-2 transition hover:bg-purple-50">
                  <span class="block text-[15px] font-semibold text-blue-600">{link.label}</span>
                  <span class="block text-[13px] text-gray-500">{link.detail}</span>
                </a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5">
        <h2 class="text-[13px] font-bold tracking-[0.08em] text-gray-500 uppercase">
          Languages <span class="text-gray-400">({languages.length})</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] text-gray-500">
          {
            totalPublished > 0
              ? `${totalPublished} translation${totalPublished === 1 ? "" : "s"} published so far.`
              : "Glossaries are up. Translations start landing on Friday."
          }
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 divide-y divide-gray-100">
          {
            languages.map(({ lang, meta, termCount, published }) => (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={`/${lang}`}
                  class="-mx-2 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-lg px-2 py-2 transition hover:bg-purple-50"
                >
                  <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                    <span class="block truncate text-[15px] font-semibold text-gray-900" lang={lang} dir={meta.dir}>
                      {meta.nativeName}
                    </span>
                    <span class="block text-[12px] text-gray-500">
                      {meta.name} &middot; {termCount} terms
                    </span>
                  </span>
                  {published > 0 && (
                    <span class="shrink-0 rounded-full bg-emerald-50 px-2 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-semibold text-emerald-700">
                      {published}
                    </span>
                  )}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </section>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>
